// Single source for the iOS app's identity and version.
//
// The release workflow does not edit this file. It passes MARKETING_VERSION and
// CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION to xcodebuild as build settings, from the git tag
// (docs/versioning-and-release-plan.md §4, §6.3). A build setting on the command line
// overrides the values below. An edit here would make `git describe --dirty` stamp the
// release as a dev build.

// The Apple Developer team. Stated here so it lives in one obvious place; the target
// build settings in project.pbxproj also carry DEVELOPMENT_TEAM (written by
// add_uitest_target.rb) and, being target-level, take precedence over this file.
TEAM_ID=S9MGTJXVTV

PRODUCT_NAME=SnapshotPB

// Deliberately NOT suffixed with $(TEAM_ID). That suffix is a project-template default
// meant to stop personal-team developers colliding on a shared identifier, but the bundle
// ID is the app's permanent App Store identity — deriving it from the team would change
// that identity the moment TEAM_ID was filled in, orphaning existing installs. TEAM_ID
// has been empty in every build to date, so this literal is byte-identical to the
// identifier the app already ships with.
PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER=com.snapshotpb.configuration.SnapshotPB

// Placeholders for local/dev builds only. A release build gets its values from xcodebuild.
// CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION is the monotonic integer the App Store requires.
CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION=1
MARKETING_VERSION=1.0
